/**
\fn pdg::Sprite::setAnimationIKTarget(uint id, number x, number y, int space)
\brief Change an IK controller's target.

Invalidates the pose so the next evaluation uses the new target. Unknown IDs, nonfinite coordinates, and invalid spaces throw.

\param id ID returned by addAnimationIK().
\param x Finite target x coordinate.
\param y Finite target y coordinate.
\param space Integer coordinate-space constant: \c pdg.animationSpace_Local (parent frame), \c pdg.animationSpace_Rig, or \c pdg.animationSpace_World (owning layer). Local uses the root bone's parent frame.

\return No value.

\see addAnimationIK(), getAnimationIKResult()
*/
